//RS //! `jet-pkg-model` — the shared, read-only package/config data model (card
//RS //! #367, D-PRODUCT-SPLIT1=C).
//RS //!
//RS //! This crate is the manifest/lock/store/ref/workspace/script *data* layer:
//RS //! parsing `package.jet`, the compiler-facing `Manifest`/`Lock` types, the C FFI
//RS //! binding-generation surface, inline script dependencies, and the read-only
//RS //! subset of the Jetpack hangar store (root resolution + listing already
//RS //! recorded entries). It holds no network/provider/shell engine code — that
//RS //! stays in the `jetpack` crate, which re-exports every module here under
//RS //! its historical paths so its own internal call sites are unchanged.
//RS //!
//RS //! `jet-driver` (the compiler's module loader) depends on this crate instead
//RS //! of the full `jetpack` engine, so the compiler's dependency graph never
//RS //! needs Jetpack's provider/network/shell machinery to resolve `use <pkg>`
//RS //! imports against already-realized packages.
//RS 
